      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: What matters most is how they appear in the inspector. When they are first made it's going to be in a very sporadic nature, just whenever a new variable is required. But when you are finished with a script and want to clean everything up, it would help if you were able to group things together logically so that when you are using the script, everything is where it should be in the inspector. To that end, it would also be nice to have the [header] attribute available as well, as that is something very useful which u# allows.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
